.TH TIMECK 8C 1/27/83
.UC 4
.SH NAME
timeck \- poll the localnet for the current time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/timeck
\%[\-s]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fItimeck\fR program sends a broadcast message to the localnet
(as defined in \fI/etc/networks\fR, see \fInetworks\fR\0(5)),
requesting the current time
(as defined in \fI/etc/services\fR, see \fIservices\fR\0(5)).
.PP
If the `\-s' option is specified,
then \fItimeck\fR will set the current host's time
to the time reported by the first host responding.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
inetd(8C)
.SH BUGS
If the local network doesn't support broadcasting,
\fItimeck\fR should consult \fI/etc/hosts\fR (see \fIhosts\fR\0(5))
and send a message to each host it finds there that resides on the
local network.
.PP
It is a feature, not a bug,
that the name and address of the local net are determined
by looking at \fI/etc/networks\fR instead of \fI/dev/kmem\fR.
